    "diagnosis": "Undifferentiated pleomorphic sarcoma of bone",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Distal femur in a 58-year-old man. Large, predominantly spindle-shaped cells with marked pleomorphism, embedded in a collagen-rich stroma. The nuclei have coarse chromatin with prominent nucleoli. Mitoses are easily seen, including atypical forms. Diffusely dispersed mild inflammatory infiltrate in the background.",
    "source": "Judith V.M.G. Bovée",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
